 ],
 "text": "Anthropic just gave Agent Skills away. 70+ AI tools now run the same skill files. Over 1M skills, nearly 280M installs. Here's why that's huge. A skill is a saved how-to your AI can actually run. Write it once, use it in Claude, ChatGPT, or Cursor. No more pasting the same prompt every morning. So here are the 5 I'd set up first. 1, inbox triage. It sorts what needs you from what doesn't. 2, meeting notes. Every call becomes a task list. 3, the weekly report. It pulls the numbers and drafts it. 4, research brief. 1 question in, sources out. 5, the daily brief. What's late, what's stuck, what needs you. And every 1 of them waits for my yes before it sends. Comment AI and I'll send you my starter pack, plus the permission sheet."
